## Project Harness

Before writing code, read `.harness/config.json`, `.harness/features.json`, `.harness/progress.md`, `.harness/handoff.md`, and the task-relevant routes in `.harness/docs-map.md`. Run `node .harness/run.mjs doctor`, `status`, and `next`.

Work on one active feature by default. Confirm any repository-defined product, security, rights, provider, or deployment gates before implementation. Use `.harness/run.mjs` for state changes. A feature may become `passing` only through successful `verify` output recorded under `.harness/evidence/`. Before ending a session, update progress and run `handoff` with the next executable step. If clean handoff requires an unauthorized commit, record that blocker instead of weakening policy.
